<h1>Iran-Linked Threat Actor Targets Nuclear Negotiators</h1>
<p class=3D"byline">By Cyber Correspondent &lt;cyberdesk@cnn.com&gt; | Updated April 19, 2024</p>
<p>A threat group attributed to Iran has been observed conducting targeted
phishing campaigns against diplomatic personnel involved in nuclear negotiations.
The campaign was first identified when traffic to 1.1.1.1 appeared in telemetry
shared with <a href=3D"https://www.cnn.com/world/middleeast">CNN World</a>.</p>
<p>Internal network scans at the affected organisation revealed a compromised
workstation at 192.168.1.100 (a private address not to be confused with
external infrastructure). The actors pivoted from that endpoint to external
command-and-control servers hosted outside the protected network.</p>
<p>Researchers at <a href=3D"https://www.cnn.com/">CNN</a> noted that the domain
<strong>www.cnn.com</strong> was used as a decoy in spear-phishing lures.
The full report is available at
<a href=3D"https://www.cnn.com/world/iran-nuclear-cyber">CNN World Iran Coverage</a>.
</p>
<figure>
<svg viewBox=3D"0 0 200 200" xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
